coder › Done on branch `work/redact-logger` (3 commits on top of `90c175f`).

What changed:
- `src/redact.ts` (new): exports `redact(value)`. Recursively copies plain objects/arrays; any key whose lowercased name contains `password`, `passwd`, `secret`, `token`, `apikey`, `api_key`, `api-key`, or `authorization` gets value `'[redacted]'` (whole value, no recursion into it); any string gets `Bearer <non-space>` → `Bearer [redacted]` via `/Bearer\s+\S+/g`. Primitives, `null`, and non-plain objects pass through unchanged. Input is never mutated — objects/arrays are rebuilt.
- `src/logger.ts`: `log()` now does `{ level, message, ...redact(fields) }` before `JSON.stringify`. One-line diff plus the `import { redact } from './redact.ts'`.
- `src/redact.test.ts` (new, 7 tests): all sensitive names/cases, nesting in objects/arrays, bearer replacement at depth, whole-value replacement for sensitive keys, passthrough of other values, no input mutation, copy identity.
- `src/logger.test.ts` (kept existing test, +3): secrets redacted, nested secrets + bearer redacted, `fields` object not mutated.

Checks — project's only check is `bun test` (`package.json` scripts: `test: bun test`, no tsconfig/lint):
